<p>"Numeric strip · densest" KPI indicator. <strong>Wide table-card layout — most data per pixel</strong>: metric / now / prev / Δ% / vs target columns. No sparkline, no chart chrome — a stripped-down 5-column grid for "spreadsheet-style" scanning when the operator wants the <em>numbers</em> and nothing else. Each row carries a tiny progress bar in the last column showing actual-vs-target as a percentage, with the percent value pinned below the bar. <strong>Wide-only by design</strong> — there's no narrow-card collapse because the row-stack form would duplicate the Comparison gauges showcase; if you need this data in a 1×3 or 25/45 cell, use Comparison gauges instead. Rendered as a <strong>table card</strong> (zero card-body padding, dividers extend edge-to-edge) so the table reads as the card's content rather than a table sitting inside another panel.</p>

<style>
/* === KPI design tokens (shared) ===
   Same palette as the other KPI showcases. Will dedupe to a shared SCSS
   module when these graduate to core. */
:root {
  --kpi-very-positive: #16a34a;
  --kpi-positive:      #22c55e;
  --kpi-neutral:       #9ca3af;
  --kpi-negative:      #ef4444;
  --kpi-very-negative: #dc2626;
  --kpi-warning:       #f97316;

  --kpi-detail-bg: rgba(15, 17, 21, 0.97);
  --kpi-detail-text: #ffffff;
  --kpi-detail-row-label: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.75);
  --kpi-detail-title: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.55);
  --kpi-detail-shadow: 0 1.4rem 3.6rem rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55);
}

/* === Card chrome === */
.kpi-strip__header {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 1.6rem;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}
.kpi-strip__live {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.6rem;
  font-family: var(--base-font-family-mono);
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--pa-text-color-1) 55%, transparent);
}
.kpi-strip__livedot {
  width: 0.8rem;
  height: 0.8rem;
  border-radius: 50%;
  background: var(--kpi-positive);
  box-shadow: 0 0 6px var(--kpi-positive);
  animation: kpiPulse 1.6s ease-in-out infinite;
}
@keyframes kpiPulse { 50% { opacity: 0.35; } }

/* Table-card mode: zero card-body padding so the table goes edge-to-edge.
   Each row carries its own horizontal padding (matches what would have
   been the body's inline padding) so the row dividers extend full-width
   to the card border. */
.kpi-strip__body { padding: 0; }

/* === Table layout ===
   Each row is its own grid sharing the same column template — this gives
   us per-row hover hosts (needed for the cursor-anchored detail popover)
   while still keeping cells aligned across rows because every row uses
   identical fr-units. Subgrid would be more semantically accurate but
   subgrid + per-row hover hosts duplicate the same effective layout in
   more lines, so we keep it simple. */
.kpi-strip__row,
.kpi-strip__head-row {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns:
    minmax(0, 2fr)      /* metric — wraps to two lines for longer labels */
    minmax(0, 1.1fr)    /* now */
    minmax(0, 1fr)      /* prev */
    minmax(0, 1fr)      /* delta */
    minmax(0, 1.6fr);   /* target (bar + pct stacked) */
  column-gap: 1.6rem;
  align-items: center;
  position: relative;
  padding: 1.1rem 1.6rem;
}
/* Divider only between data rows / between head and first row.
   Adjacent-sibling combinator keeps this resilient if a tile gets
   added or reordered. */
.kpi-strip__row + .kpi-strip__row,
.kpi-strip__head-row + .kpi-strip__row {
  border-top: 1px solid var(--pa-border-color);
}

/* Header cells — uppercase mono labels at low contrast.
   Right-aligned for the numeric columns so the header matches the
   right-aligned values below. */
.kpi-strip__head {
  font-family: var(--base-font-family-mono);
  font-size: 1.1rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--pa-text-color-1) 42%, transparent);
}
.kpi-strip__head--num { text-align: end; }

/* Metric label — uppercase mono, slightly less prominent than NOW.
   Allowed to wrap to two lines so the column doesn't have to be
   ridiculously wide for "MONTHLY REVENUE" vs "NPS". */
.kpi-strip__metric {
  font-family: var(--base-font-family-mono);
  font-size: 1.4rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--pa-text-color-1) 78%, transparent);
  line-height: 1.2;
}

/* NOW — the focal value. Bigger than everything else in the row. */
.kpi-strip__now {
  font-family: var(--base-font-family-mono);
  font-size: 1.8rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  text-align: end;
  display: flex;
  align-items: baseline;
  justify-content: flex-end;
  color: var(--pa-text-color-1);
  white-space: nowrap;
  line-height: 1;
}
.kpi-strip__now .kpi-strip__num { font-weight: 700; }
.kpi-strip__now .kpi-strip__unit {
  font-size: 1.1rem;
  font-weight: 500;
  color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--pa-text-color-1) 50%, transparent);
  margin: 0 0.2rem;
}

/* PREV — same scale as Δ but at lower contrast (it's reference data,
   the eye should jump past it to NOW and Δ). */
.kpi-strip__prev {
  font-family: var(--base-font-family-mono);
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  font-weight: 500;
  color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--pa-text-color-1) 42%, transparent);
  text-align: end;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

/* Δ% — coloured by sentiment, same 5-step palette as the rest of the
   showcase pages. Same kpi-strip__delta--{positive | negative | up-strong | ...}
   class surface. */
.kpi-strip__delta {
  font-family: var(--base-font-family-mono);
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  text-align: end;
  white-space: nowrap;
  --kpi-strip-delta-color: var(--kpi-positive);
  color: var(--kpi-strip-delta-color);
}
.kpi-strip__delta--positive    { --kpi-strip-delta-color: var(--kpi-positive); }
.kpi-strip__delta--negative    { --kpi-strip-delta-color: var(--kpi-negative); }
.kpi-strip__delta--neutral     { --kpi-strip-delta-color: var(--kpi-neutral); }
.kpi-strip__delta--up-strong   { --kpi-strip-delta-color: var(--kpi-very-positive); }
.kpi-strip__delta--down-strong { --kpi-strip-delta-color: var(--kpi-very-negative); }

/* VS TARGET — bar + percent stacked. Bar fills horizontally; percent
   pinned to the bar's right edge below it. Fill is theme-neutral grey
   (not sentiment-coloured) — the *pct value* signals overshoot/undershoot
   and the eye reads "97" vs "108" vs "54" without needing colour to
   reinforce it. Bar fill is capped at 100% visually so an over-target
   metric still reads as "fully filled" rather than overflowing the
   container; the actual pct value (e.g. 108%) shows in the label below. */
.kpi-strip__target {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.35rem;
}
.kpi-strip__bar {
  position: relative;
  height: 0.5rem;
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--pa-text-color-1) 12%, transparent);
  overflow: hidden;
  border-radius: 0.1rem;
}
.kpi-strip__fill {
  position: absolute;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  bottom: 0;
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--pa-text-color-1) 40%, transparent);
}
.kpi-strip__bar-pct {
  font-family: var(--base-font-family-mono);
  font-size: 1.05rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--pa-text-color-1) 55%, transparent);
  align-self: flex-end;
  line-height: 1;
}

/* Hover host: subtle highlight on a row when the cursor is over it,
   so the popover that follows the cursor has a clear "this row" anchor. */
.kpi-strip__row:hover {
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--pa-text-color-1) 4%, transparent);
}

/* Modifier: drop the PREV column. 4-col layout (metric / now / Δ% / target).
   Useful in narrow placements where there isn't room for prev *and* now
   side-by-side. The card's markup omits the prev cells; this rule just
   resets the column template so the remaining 4 cells fit cleanly. */
.kpi-strip--no-prev .kpi-strip__row,
.kpi-strip--no-prev .kpi-strip__head-row {
  grid-template-columns:
    minmax(0, 2fr)      /* metric */
    minmax(0, 1.1fr)    /* now */
    minmax(0, 1fr)      /* delta */
    minmax(0, 1.6fr);   /* target */
}

/* === Footer caption === */
.kpi-strip__footer {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: center;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 1rem;
  font-family: var(--base-font-family-mono);
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--pa-text-color-1) 55%, transparent);
}
.kpi-strip__footer strong {
  color: var(--pa-text-color-1);
  font-weight: 700;
}

/* === Hover detail popover (cursor-anchored, same recipe as elsewhere) === */
.kpi-strip-detail {
  position: fixed;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  visibility: hidden;
  pointer-events: none;
  z-index: 9000;
  min-width: 24rem;
  max-width: 30rem;
  background: var(--kpi-detail-bg);
  color: var(--kpi-detail-text);
  padding: 1.1rem 1.4rem;
  font-family: var(--base-font-family-mono);
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  line-height: 1.5;
  border-radius: 0.4rem;
  box-shadow: var(--kpi-detail-shadow);
}
.kpi-strip-detail[data-show] { visibility: visible; }
.kpi-strip-detail-title {
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  font-size: 1.05rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--kpi-detail-title);
  margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
}
.kpi-strip-detail dl {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
  gap: 0.35rem 1.6rem;
  margin: 0;
}
.kpi-strip-detail dt { margin: 0; color: var(--kpi-detail-row-label); font-weight: 400; }
.kpi-strip-detail dd { margin: 0; text-align: end; font-weight: 600; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
.kpi-strip-detail .pos { color: var(--kpi-positive); }
.kpi-strip-detail .neg { color: var(--kpi-negative); }
.kpi-strip-detail .warn { color: var(--kpi-warning); }
</style>

